<title>USA: Fujitsu gets Hart-Scott early termination.</title>
<headline>Fujitsu gets Hart-Scott early termination.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fujitsu Ltd said the U.S. Department of Justice and the U.S. Federal Trade Commission granted it early termination of the waiting period under the Hart-Scott-Rodino Antitrust Improvements Act for its offer to buy Amdahl Corp.</p>
<p>Early termination indicates that those government agencies do not intend to oppose the tender offer and related merger on antitrust grounds, it said.</p>
<p>The tender offer, for $12 per share, is still subject to certain other conditions and is scheduled to expire September 5.</p>
</text>
